    "basicInfo": "East of the Fálgarr Marches the tree-line breaks into a vast rolling country of golden grass, forested plateaus, and painted canyons — the homeland the beastkin peoples call the Sunmane Steppe, and among themselves Tír na Rua, the Red Land. Here the cat-kin, wolf-kin, fox-kin, rabbit-kin, bird-kin and their many cousins are not a scattered minority in someone else's cities but a people at home: organized into clans, governed by a great Moot rather than a crown, and bound by hunt-right, guest-right, and blood. The clans range their herds across the plains, keep arboreal holds in the plateau woods, and gather each season at the Moot Hollow to settle debts, arrange marriages, and argue the future of a people the mortal kingdoms have never quite known what to do with. Outsiders are watched, tested, and — if they honor the old courtesies — fed.",
