  "Heartgate Basin": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — sacred fox-spirit garden-forest; the developed heart of the Demi-Plane. The heart of the Demi-Plane — the developed core that grew outward from the first clearing. Home to The Gateway Clearing, the gateway chamber, and the Chamberlain's quarters. The Hearth Springs, Mana Heart, and Verdant Plot surround the basin's grounds. This is where every expansion begins and where the Chamberlain receives the creator. The Heartgate Basin is not part of any mortal geography: it is reached ONLY by the Demi-Plane Gate ability or the Demi-Plane Anchor item — no road, ship, spell, or teleportation circle arrives without the creator's permission. The Chamberlain manages day-to-day operations here and reports on the dimension's state.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 1–12): garden spirits tending the grounds uninvited and unthanked, foxfire wisps drifting along the formal paths, tame spirit fauna that treat the basin as one great garden, and harmless mana elementals that pool in sunlit corners like warm curiously-shaped dust. Nothing here threatens; the heart's defenses are elsewhere.\n\nResources: mana fruit from the basin's groves, cultivated herbs, spirit flowers that bloom in response to company, and garden materials — cut stone, clean gravel, spring water — all cheerfully provided.\n\nKnown Locations (all established and marked): The Gateway Clearing with its Demi-Plane Gate and Gateway Chamber; the Chamberlain's Quarters; the Hearth Springs; the Mana Heart; and the Verdant Plot. The basin is the dimension's administrative heart: discoveries here stay hidden, small, and personal — a thought left in the garden, a stone rearranged overnight, a wisp that learned a name — rather than major wilderness sites.",
