  "The Still Frontier": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — cold highland spirit-forest; pale conifers with frost-glinting needles under strange weather (silver breath-mist, frost-formed foxfire in the pines, snow that falls in slow spirals). The far northwest edge of the Demi-Plane — where the dimension's influence thins and the ground becomes hesitant. The sky is paler, the air quieter. The world simply stops, not with a wall but with a fading: ground grows indistinct, colors wash toward grey, sound carries strangely. The Chamberlain calls this the frontier — the limit of what has been willed into existence. Beyond it is nothing, merely the absence of intention. When the creator is ready to expand, expansion begins here.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 20–30): frost foxes trotting the ridgelines, snow wraiths drifting between the pines in slow silence, pale wolves pacing the forest's edge, and cold spirits pooled in the hollows like standing frost. The dimension's most serious wilderness: everything here is healthy, wild, and stronger than it looks.\n\nResources: frostwood from the pale conifers, ice crystal formed at the forest's still ponds, winter herbs under the snow-line, and frozen foxfire gathered from the frost-formed motes in the pines.\n\nKnown Locations: the Frontier Fade — the misted rim where willed ground becomes unwilled — and Frostpine Ridge, the high spine of pale conifers. Everything colder stays unmarked: hidden caves under the roots, frozen shrines iced mid-ceremony, strange weather pockets that never move, and powerful roaming creatures cross the frontier as discoveries, not permanent markers.",
    "factions": [],
    "hiddenInfo": "The frontier shifts — advancing as the Demi-Plane's ambient potential seeps outward, retreating when its mana runs low. The Chamberlain reads its position as a health indicator: stable means equilibrium, advancing means growth, retreating means something is draining the dimension.",
