  "The Pale Reaches": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — misty white-stone highland badland; low pale rock benches, shallow valleys of glowing silver fog, lichen that lights faintly like constellations underfoot. A vast stretch of near-featureless terrain north of the developed core — low hills of white-grey stone, shallow mist-filled valleys, a sky that shifts between dawn light and featureless silver. Nothing lives here yet, but the ground has texture: it is waiting, not empty. The Demi-Plane's largest reserve of undeveloped potential — a place where a forest, a river, or a city could be raised if someone chose it.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 18–30): fog elementals congealing in the valley mists, pale stone beasts standing among the benches until approached, silver wisps tracing the fog lines, and ghostlike temporary creatures — half-formed visitors made of potential, never the same twice. Nothing here is fully committed to being.\n\nResources: silver lichen lighting the benches like constellations, white stone cut clean from the hills, condensed dimensional mist gathered at dawn, and pale crystals formed where fog has pooled longest.\n\nKnown Locations: the Ghost Valleys — the mist-filled shallow valleys where potential behaves most freely — and the Silver-Lichen Flats, the broad benches of lit stone. Everything else stays provisional on purpose: raw dimensional potential here briefly creates landscapes, structures, bridges, settlements, and encounters that dissolve again. These ghost-landscapes should be met as discoveries and sometimes never return — they are not permanent map markers, and the Reaches resists being fully cataloged by design.",
    "factions": [],
    "hiddenInfo": "The valley mist is raw dimensional potential in semi-tangible form. Focused intent makes it coalesce into whatever is imagined; uncontrolled, it forms fleeting ghost-landscapes that dissolve in seconds — sometimes matching places the creator has seen or dreamed.",
