  "The North Field": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — boreal river-grass plain; flat wet-grassland crossed by slow shining channels that appear and vanish; windswept ribbon-cloud skies, and rain that falls upward in glittering curtains. A broad plain stretching north from the heart of the Demi-Plane — flat, windswept, quiet. The ground is firmer than the Pale Reaches, as if the dimension has already decided this will be something solid. A faint scentless wind blows from the north. This region feels like it is waiting for a purpose — farmland, a great hall, an arena. The most natural-feeling of the undeveloped zones, as if the world wants it inhabited, with luminous reed-seeds drifting like slow lanterns at dusk.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 8–20): reed elk wading the shining channels, wind sprites riding the scentless north wind, wetland birds in vast restless flocks, and channel serpents gliding beneath the slow water — curious rather than hostile, but large enough to demand respect.\n\nResources: rivergrass cut from the channel banks, luminous reed-seeds drifting at dusk, freshwater herbs, and mana-rich silt dredged gently from the channel beds.\n\nKnown Locations: the Shining Channels — the appearing-and-vanishing waterways — and the Northwind Plain, the broad waiting heart of the region. The watercourses shift naturally, so the Field rewards wandering: hidden ponds, spirit crossings, isolated groves, and temporary channels appear and reroute on their own. Nothing rewards a fixed map; everything rewards a good walk.",
    "factions": [],
    "hiddenInfo": "The north wind is the Demi-Plane breathing — ambient mana circulating through the expanding body of the dimension. Strong infrastructure makes the wind gentle and constant; strained infrastructure makes it stop. The Chamberlain checks this wind before every health report.",
