  "The Fold": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — folded scrub-steppe; grassy wave-terraces of spatial strangeness; grass, heath, and low stone rise and repeat in paper-fold patterns. A region where terrain folds inward on itself — ridges that curve like folded paper, valleys that loop back on their own paths, ground rising and falling in waves rather than slopes. Disorienting but not dangerous: simply unfinished, the dimension's unresolved experiment with elevation. Fascinating for anyone interested in how the Demi-Plane thinks about space.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 15–28): loop hounds coursing along paths that always bring them back, fold sprites folded neatly into creases of ground, warped stone beasts lumbering between non-adjacent slopes, and spatial wisps drifting sideways out of nowhere. Nothing hunts by force; everything hunts by geometry.\n\nResources: warped stone, spatial crystal, strange herbs that grow in two places at once, and foldglass — thin panes that show the other side of a ridge from the harmless side.\n\nKnown Locations: the Folding Ridges — the paper-fold uplands themselves — and the Returning Valley, the loop-back valley floor at the Fold's heart. Everything else stays unknown until earned: paths here loop and return walkers to earlier places without their noticing. Hidden pockets, impossible caves, and spatial shortcuts become known only after successful exploration — a region where experience of the ground, not documentation of it, is the true map.",
    "factions": [],
    "hiddenInfo": "The warped geometry is a natural defense. Intruders entering without permission become lost — folding paths turn them around without their realizing it. The Chamberlain considers the Fold an accidental blessing and recommends not 'fixing' it before the creator understands what it does.",
