  "The Veiled Edge": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — luminous boundary-scrub; low silvered spirit-grass fading into a shimmering fog-edge under strange weather (slow-lit aurora ground-glow that ripples where the veil is touched). The far northeast corner of the Demi-Plane — where the dimension meets its own boundary in a soft curtain of shimmering light. Not a wall but a veil: translucent, faintly luminous, cool to the touch. Beyond it nothing is visible. The veil ripples when approached, as if acknowledging presence. Here the Demi-Plane ends and the void between dimensions begins — not hostile, simply other. The Chamberlain finds it peaceful; others find it unsettling.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 22–30): veil moths with wings of translucent membrane that pass through the veil without breaking it; aurora wisps drifting along the boundary, feeding on light leaking through; boundary spirits — old, calm, and rarely seen — who walk the edge as if patrolling; and, on rare nights, void-adjacent entities glimpsed only as pressure and absence at the perimeter. Nothing here is aggressive; everything is older than the dimension itself.\n\nResources: veilglass — thin, flawless panes of crystallized boundary that hum when struck; aurora crystal, which stores light the way ice stores cold; silver spirit-grass, the region's staple fiber; and boundary essence, a faint residue of the veil itself, gathered only where it ripples.\n\nKnown Locations (established and marked): The Shimmering Curtain — the veil's most luminous reach, where the boundary glows brightest; and Veilwatch Point — a low stone rise offering the clearest view of the edge.",
    "hiddenInfo": "The veil is permeable under specific conditions. Focused intent thins it, allowing a view of the space between dimensions — mortal leylines, distant pocket dimensions, the vast emptiness separating realities. The Chamberlain does not know this. The creator has not tried.",
