  "The First Meadow": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — luminous wildflower meadow; rolling grassland where self-seeded foxfire-blooms, silver-green grasses, and flowers that turn to follow warmth; pollen drift rises in slow spirals at dawn and settles like warm snow at dusk. A transitional region between the developed core and the northern wilds — rolling silver-green grassland that has begun to self-generate without the creator's direct intervention. Wildflowers appear in clusters the Chamberlain swears were never planted. This is the Demi-Plane learning to grow on its own — the sign of a pocket dimension becoming self-sustaining. The First Meadow also carries the Beginning's Torii at its northwest edge: a vermilion gate rising from the unmarked grass as the First Meadow path turns toward the Veiled Fox Sanctuary, marking the crossing into the sanctuary. Beyond it, the shape of the sanctuary can be glimpsed — fox-spirit nature visible from the meadow — but crossing is by invitation only. Tsukiko passes freely. No road continues past the torii for anyone else.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 1–10): flower sprites riding the pollen spirals, meadow foxes napping in the grass, spirit butterflies in slow migrating clouds, and harmless grazing animals that arrived from somewhere and stayed. The region's gentlest ground outside the Southroll.\n\nResources: foxfire blooms, meadow herbs, luminous pollen collected at dawn, and silver-green grass cut in woven sheaves.\n\nKnown Locations: the Beginning's Torii at the meadow's northwest edge — the crossing into the Veiled Fox Sanctuary — with the Fox Statues seated on either side, and the Sanctuary Approach, the path leading to it. The wider meadow stays bright and uncluttered: hidden flower circles, tiny spirit shrines, and seasonal phenomena appear as small discoveries, never as map markers.",
    "factions": [],
    "hiddenInfo": "The self-generating grass measures the Demi-Plane's autonomy. A dimension that can sustain basic life without constant creator attention is approaching the threshold where it could survive the creator's temporary absence without collapsing. The Chamberlain tracks grass growth as a maturity metric. The Beginning's Torii appeared the same morning the sanctuary did — with fox statues sitting on either side the way a household sets out garden kami, and a faint smell of sugared ginger that never quite fades.",
