  "The Stone Rise": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — rocky moss-highland; grey-stone hills with hardy moss and lichen-terraces, cooler air, mineral springs. A rocky upland northeast of the developed core — the Demi-Plane's first successful experiment with elevation. Rolling hills of grey stone covered in hardy moss, outcroppings with views across the entire dimension on clear days. The air is thinner, cooler, faintly mineral. The Stone Rise feels old despite the Demi-Plane being young, as if the dimension pulled the idea of mountains from somewhere deep.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 8–20): cliff drakes roosting in the high crags, stone sprites that rearrange scree for their own reasons, mountain goats cropping the moss-terraces, and mineral elementals rising briefly from the richest ore seams. Terrain makes every encounter a position problem.\n\nResources: iron-rich stone, spirit minerals, lichen, and mineral water from the springs — all harvestable at scale once mining begins.\n\nKnown Locations: the Mineral Springs — the upland's flowing veins — the High Outlook, the great outcropping that sees the whole dimension, and Foundation Ridge, the ridgeline the dimension rests on. Beyond these, the upland is deliberately unmapped: numerous caves, narrow passes, hidden chambers, rock formations and mining prospects exist until an explorer names them. The best region in the Demi-Plane for mines, vaults, and views.",
    "factions": [],
    "hiddenInfo": "The Stone Rise is the Demi-Plane's structural foundation — bedrock on which the rest of the dimension is built. Destabilizing it would set the whole dimension drifting. The Chamberlain does not know this; the Mana Heart's guardian entity does, and patrols the perimeter when not watching its post.",
