  "The Mirror Mere": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — twilight wetland; still pools connected by gentle channels, reed-beds, water that glows faintly and holds reflection as if it remembers what stood before it; fish-sized lights drift beneath the surface, never quite taking shape. Twilight forever. A region of low, still water northeast of the developed core — shallow pools connected by gentle channels, reflecting a sky that is forever twilight here. The water is calm, clear, faintly luminous. The Mirror Mere is a place for reflection in both senses: the Demi-Plane created water here before anyone asked, as if it understood that a world needs somewhere to look at itself.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 10–22): mirror fish rising like slow silver thought, luminous amphibians calling across the channels, water spirits combing the reed-beds, and reflection wisps that drift along the surface duplicating the stillness. Everything here is halved: seen, and seen again.\n\nResources: spirit pearls formed on the pools' oldest beds, luminous reeds, mana-water ladled without disturbing the calm, and mirror-lotus blooming where two reflections agree.\n\nKnown Locations: the Twilight Pools — the heart of the Mere's still water — and the Reflection Basin, the largest single mirror of all. The rest stays unmarked: reflections here can lead somewhere. Hidden islands surface in the shallows, submerged ruins show through clear water on quiet days, temporary spirit paths open across channels at dusk, and visions stand whole in the still water for those patient enough to look twice. Not every pool or island is found — only the ones that find you.",
    "factions": [],
    "hiddenInfo": "The Mere acts as the mana circulation's reservoir and regulator — absorbing excess during peaks, releasing it during lulls. Surface stillness is a literal indicator: ripples mean turbulent flow, calm means stable. The Chamberlain checks the surface before every report.",
