  "The Westreach": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — open mixed grassland; rolling ground with scattered young trees, wild cowslip and red sorrel, and well-drained soils suited to building; dew here beads into tiny foxfire beads that hum faintly at dawn. The western approach to the developed core — open grassland with scattered young trees and the faint impression of roads not yet built. The ground is firm and well-drained, the most practical terrain in the Demi-Plane for future construction. The Chamberlain has marked sites for a market square, a guest house, a training yard — but nothing rises here without the creator's word. The Westreach is ready and waiting.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 1–10): young treants swaying among the sapling trees, meadow animals in loose herds, harmless sprites riding the dawn foxfire beads, and occasional territorial spirit beasts that draw a line across good grass and defend it more from habit than malice. The safest wild ground in the dimension.\n\nResources: timber from the young groves (never more than the land gives gladly), common herbs, fertile soil, and foxfire dew collected at first light.\n\nKnown Locations: three taped stakes mark the Future Market Square, the Guesthouse Site, and the Training Yard Site — the Chamberlain's staged expansion plots. Most of the Westreach is deliberately left open ground so construction, when it comes, matters. Small groves, natural wells, roadside shrines, and minor discoveries arise on their own along the faint impressions of roads the dimension is already imagining.",
    "factions": [],
    "hiddenInfo": "Westreach soil is the most responsive in the Demi-Plane — it shifts and settles to accommodate construction faster than anywhere else. Buildings take hold in days rather than weeks, because the region sits directly in the mana flow's primary western channel, receiving more raw potential than any other.",
