  "The Hollow Vale": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — sheltered terraced vale; gentle valley slopes, stone terraces, still air; foxfire motes settle along the terrace edges like lanterns placed by unseen hands. The southern approach to the developed core — a gentle valley sloping down through terraces the Demi-Plane formed on its own, each wide and flat and waiting for purpose. Sheltered from the ambient wind by surrounding terrain, it is the calmest region in the dimension. The Chamberlain suggests it as ideal for future residential expansion: protected, quiet, close to the core.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 4–14): terrace sprites keeping tidy watch along the stone rims, burrowing spirit rabbits in the soft terrace banks, songbirds that arrive from no direction and leave the same way, and minor earth spirits that smooth a cracked terrace wall overnight. All gentle; most can be befriended with patience and a handful of herbs.\n\nResources: spirit clay from the terrace banks, terrace herbs, medicinal roots, and foxfire moss that grows along the shadiest terrace walls.\n\nKnown Locations: the Residential Terraces — the wide stone shelves awaiting future homes — and the Sheltered Vale, the calm valley floor between them. Most terraces are deliberately left empty and unmarked for future development. Small caves, hidden springs, abandoned spirit shelters, and natural viewpoints dot the slopes for those who walk them rather than read them.",
    "factions": [],
    "hiddenInfo": "The terraces match the dimensions of rooms in the Hidden Estate — as if the dimension were trying to build a home on a grander scale. The Chamberlain noticed the pattern but has not mentioned it, unsure whether the creator would find it touching or unsettling.",
