  "The Deep Expanse": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — vast prairie plain; flat firm ground, tall blue-green grasses in slow waves, a high clear sky; the grass hums almost audibly when the wind passes through it. The southern frontier — a vast open expanse mirroring the Gateway Clearing's original potential at a grander scale. Flat firm ground, a high clear sky, an overwhelming sense of possibility. The largest single region in the Demi-Plane, entirely undeveloped: a blank canvas the size of a small country. The Chamberlain dreams of what could be built here. The creator has not yet visited.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 10–22): prairie drakes skimming low over the grass in territory-display flights, mana antelope herds that shimmer faintly with stored potential, wind spirits rolling across the plain as slow spirals, and large grazing spirit-beasts — silent, herd-minded giants found only in the deep grass. Distances mean no encounter is ever an ambush unless intended.\n\nResources: mana amber wept onto grass roots, tallgrass herbs, beast materials from the drakes and antelope, and windseed gathered on high-wind days.\n\nKnown Locations: the Great Prairie — the endless open ground itself — and the Mana-Density Survey Point, the Chamberlain's quiet measuring stone. Everything deeper is deliberately unmarked. A region this vast can hold hidden monster territories, ancient-looking stones, underground chambers, and wandering events without any marker: discoveries here arrive by walking through grass taller than a rider.",
    "factions": [],
    "hiddenInfo": "After the Easthold, the Deep Expanse holds the deepest mana reserves — still rather than pressing, like a reservoir awaiting a tap. A city, a forest, a mountain range would draw from it. The Chamberlain keeps a hand-drawn mana-density map in their quarters, waiting for the day the creator asks.",
