  "The Rift March": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — broken marchland; dark stone clefts and ridges between grassland, deep rifts, shadowed stone; cold blue light seeps up from the rifts at night, and echoes return late by a heartbeat. The far southeast corner — a region of sharp contrast: soft grassland fading westward into the Southroll, dropping eastward into dark stone and deep clefts, as if two ideas of terrain collided and neither won. The most dramatic and most unsettled undeveloped landscape. The Chamberlain avoids the eastern half without a reason.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 18–30): rift crawlers descending the fissure walls head-first, stone predators blended into the dark ridges, blue-flame wisps luring along the cleft rims at night, and cave drakes roosting in the deeper systems. The genuinely dangerous ground begins east of the cleft ridgeline.\n\nResources: rift crystal, darkstone, blue mana ore, and deep fungi grown on the rift walls' cold light.\n\nKnown Locations: the Eastern Clefts — the great dark fissure system — and the Rift Overlook, the grassland rim that watches them. Beyond that, nothing is marked on purpose. This is the region the Chamberlain believes will hold the Demi-Plane's dungeon if it ever grows one: unmapped caves, deep fissures, monster nests, strange ruins, and possible dungeon entrances belong to the clefts' unrecorded depths, found by explorers or not at all.",
    "factions": [],
    "hiddenInfo": "The dark terrain grew from the creator's unspoken fears rather than hopes — not hostile, but uncomfortable. The clefts lead toward the dimensional boundary; standing at the bottom of one feels like standing at the bottom of the world. If the Demi-Plane ever develops a dungeon or dangerous region, the Chamberlain suspects it will be here — and is not sure that would be bad.",
