  "The Dim March": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — hushed moss-hollow; soft pale moss ground, dim even light, restful still air; the moss hears footsteps and dims them to nothing, keeping silence undisturbed. The southwest boundary of the Demi-Plane — the quietest corner. Soft ground covered in fine pale moss, still cool air, dim even light like a room lit by candles. No feature distinguishes one direction from another. The Dim March is not unsettling, simply calm in a way that makes everything else feel loud. The Chamberlain comes here to think without interruption.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 18–28): hush-wisps drifting between the moss hummocks, pale moss spirits folded into the ground itself, silent moths that follow movement without sound, and dormant shade-beasts sleeping beneath the deeper moss banks — all passive unless disturbed. Most wildlife never rouses; what does is drawn to noise, not presence.\n\nResources: stillmoss cut in intact sheets, preservation moss from the deepest hollows, muted spirit-stone nodules, and silence-thread fungi growing along old mana seams.\n\nKnown Locations: Candle Hollow — a soft-floored hollow where the dim light pools brightest, the region's one named landmark; the Chamberlain's Emergency Cache is kept somewhere beneath the moss (its exact site is not marked and is known only to him). The rest of the march is deliberately unmarked: hidden storage hollows, old mana pockets, and things preserved unnaturally well wait to be discovered beneath the moss by those who explore patiently.",
    "factions": [],
    "hiddenInfo": "The dimness is mana in a resting state — so still it produces no light or warmth. This makes the region the dimension's best storage zone: anything placed here changes less than elsewhere. Food stays fresh, materials hold their form, enchantments persist longer. The Chamberlain has already quietly begun storing emergency supplies here.",
    "images": {
      "map": {
        "crop": {
          "focus": {
            "x": 50,
            "y": 50
          },
