  "The Open Horizon": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — endless flat savanna; open level ground beneath an enormous sky. The far south — vast flat ground beneath an enormous sky, horizon visible in every direction. The Demi-Plane at its most open: no hills, no trees, no structures, just ground and sky and the faint hum of potential; the horizon line glows faintly warm, like embers at the world's edge. The Chamberlain describes it as the dimension's invitation — the Demi-Plane showing the creator exactly how much room there is to build. Not empty. Generous.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 10–20): wind hares bounding across the grass, prairie deer in loose herds, small sky spirits that drift at eye-height on still afternoons, and wandering mana birds that follow invisible currents of potential. All shy; all visible for kilometers against the flat.\n\nResources: horizon grass, windseed gathered from grass-tops, sun-dried herbs, and ambient mana crystals strewn thinly across the plain.\n\nKnown Locations: Skywatch Rise — the region's one gentle rise, its landmark and watchpoint; and the Open Horizon Plain, the great open ground itself. Everything else is deliberately unmarked. In emptiness this total, any new camp, ruin, strange object, or natural wonder should feel significant precisely because of the nothing around it — such discoveries are made by crossing the plain, not by consulting a map.",
    "factions": [],
    "hiddenInfo": "The flatness is a slate with no bias, no tendency, no half-formed ideas — it becomes exactly what the creator intends, nothing more or less. Powerful and demanding alike: vague intention yields vague results, precise intention yields perfect ones. The Chamberlain has advised waiting for a clear vision before developing here.",
