  "The Last Edge": {
    "basicInfo": "Biome — still stony plain; smooth flat ground, motionless air, steady grey light; nothing here has a shadow — light falls without direction. The far southeast corner — the dimension's end. Where other boundaries fade, fog, or shimmer, the Last Edge is simply still: smooth flat ground, motionless air, steady even grey light. No drama, no mystery, no veil — just the quiet certainty that here the world ends and nothing else begins. The Chamberlain finds it peaceful; most find it profound. The creator has not visited yet, but the Chamberlain believes they should.\n\nWildlife & Encounters (levels 25–30): almost none by design. Rarely, an anchor sentinel — a tall grey figure that stands watch for exactly one night and is gone — or a silent dimensional spirit passes through without acknowledgment. Nothing here hunts, gathers, or nests. Any creature found on the Edge is behaving strangely, which makes it important.\n\nResources: nullstone, grey crystal, and fixed-point fragments — all scarce, all worth carrying, all found only after long walking.\n\nKnown Locations: The Last Edge itself — the barren rim of the dimension — and the Dimensional Anchor Point. Everything else stays deliberately barren and unmarked. Discoveries here should be rare and important: strange geometric formations with no origin, anchor phenomena, or remnants that should not logically exist in a young pocket dimension — a weathered coin, a foundation stone, a child's toy half-buried in smooth grey ground.",
    "factions": [],
    "hiddenInfo": "The Last Edge is the Demi-Plane's anchor point — the single fixed coordinate from which the entire dimension is extrapolated. Destabilizing it would not collapse the dimension but set it drifting silently until it lost connection to the mortal world. The Chamberlain does not know; the Mana Heart's guardian entity does, and extends its patrol here whenever the creator is absent.",
